# Camera bus (plan #656): interval stills are local artifacts
stills/

# bench scene renders (regenerate with: sim.bench_scene --render DIR)
scene_render/
bench_views/

# Edge-validation cache: derived from poses.json + the model, and keyed
# by their contents. Rebuildable, machine-specific, and would churn on
# every routine run.
.edge-cache.json

# Bench traces. Regenerated by `hardware.bench.batch --out runs/` and by
# `exercise --trace`, machine-specific, and some are 100 kB a piece. The
# NUMBERS that matter out of a run belong in a plan or a doc, not as a CSV
# nobody can interpret a year later.
runs/
run*.csv

# Local scratch, deliberately never committed. Two kinds, both of which
# accumulated on cell1 until Kyle asked for the rule (2026-07-29):
#   _*.py           throwaway probes (_dyn.py printed twin masses once)
#   docs/reviews/   pastes Kyle drops for an agent to read - a bug message,
#                   a stack trace. A drop zone, not a docs section.
# Config that would be needed to REBUILD a cell is the opposite of this and
# must be committed - home.json was untracked for days for want of this
# distinction, and nothing regenerates it.
_*.py
# ...but _*.py also matches __init__.py, which silently un-tracks the
# package marker of every NEW package. The existing ones survive only
# because they were tracked before this rule landed, and the breakage is
# invisible locally: the file is right there on disk, so imports work for
# you and fail for a fresh clone. Same shape as the home.json case above.
!__init__.py
!__main__.py
docs/reviews/
